From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] feat(share): share-link guests: a name, an optional
 password, the link's level

Reviewers without a doop account had no way in past looking: a link's
comment and edit levels need an account, and with sign-up closed every
reviewer meant an account made by hand. Review tools that send links
(Frame.io review links, InVision share links) ask a visitor for a name
and, when the owner wants one, a password. This does the same, and leaves
both choices to the owner.

- The owner picks the link's level (view, comment, review or edit; review
  is new as a link level) and, optionally, a password: the Share dialog,
  PATCH /api/canvases/:id { linkAccess, linkPassword } (null or '' removes
  it), or PUT /api/operator/canvases/:id/link { access, password }. With
  FULL_UI off the owner gets Share back (the dock, the phone menu, the
  canvas tile menu); the community listing stays put away.
- The hash (better-auth's scrypt) is canvases.link_password (migration
  0050) and stays on the server (linkPasswords.ts); the Canvas object
  carries only the flag. A link with a password admits nobody by itself,
  signed out or signed in.
- A signed-out visitor on a link that asks for a password, or grants more
  than a look, gets a door (LinkJoin): a name, the password if any. "Just
  look" stays for links without one. POST /api/auth/link/session (behind
  formCsrfMiddleware; 10 wrong tries per visitor or 100 per canvas in 15
  minutes answer 429) makes a shadow user under .embed.invalid with the
  typed name and a 30-day session whose grant is on the session row
  (link_canvas_id, link_key = the password's fingerprint).
- The role is read live (linkRole): a level change applies at once, the
  link off shuts guests out, and a new or removed password ends every
  earlier guest session (rows deleted, room closed with 4403).
- A guest reaches its canvas and nothing account-wide (linkRouteAllowed):
  the canvas's routes and its frames', comments', tasks' and feedback's,
  minus claim, duplicate, workspace, members, sync keys, GitHub, publish
  and the canvas's own PATCH/DELETE; never the canvas list, new canvases
  or agent keys. /api/me says linkGuest; the app keeps the session on its
  canvas (anywhere else signs it out) and the dock drops back, settings,
  Share and Connect AI for it.

Tests: shareLink.test.ts (real server, 12 tests: the flag and no hash on
the wire, owner-only, nobody in by the link alone, name and password
checks, confinement, live level changes up to edit, a new password and
the link off shutting guests out, name-only links, the operator API, the
throttle). With it 19 related files pass (access, guestCanvas,
shareLinkRoles, operator, embed, reviewVerdicts, i18n, admin...). In a
browser against a production build: the owner sets Comment and a
password from the dock, a fresh browser gets the door, a wrong password
is refused, the right one opens the reviewer layout as the typed name,
the comment lands, and leaving the canvas brings the door back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
